Write the narrative parts of a short incident postmortem for business and engineering readers.
Use ONLY the facts below. Do NOT include any numbers for money, percentages, durations or counts (the report
fills those in from computed data); deploy tags and config key names are fine.
Return ONLY a JSON object: {"summary": "2-3 sentences", "root_cause": "2-4 sentences", "follow_ups": ["3 short items"]}

FACTS:
{"incident": "INC-0001", "signal": "Shop memory rising 178 MB/min (now 145 MB)", "service": "shop", "status": "Resolved", "bad_deploy": "deploy-6", "last_good_deploy": "deploy-5", "decision": {"hypotheses": [{"cause": "Deploy-6 introduced an unbounded session cache in app/main.py causing memory growth (tr-4, KB:PM-03, KB:RB-04)", "confidence": 1.0, "evidence": ["tr-1", "tr-2", "tr-3", "tr-4", "tr-7"]}], "chosen_action": "rollback_deploy", "rationale": "Since the restart only temporarily mitigated the symptom and memory continues to climb due to the code change in deploy-6, we must roll back to the last good deploy (deploy-5) per policy and KB:RB-04.", "expected_effect": "Reverts production to deploy-5, removing the unbounded session cache in deploy-6 and stopping memory growth.", "risk": "Low risk rollback to a stable previous deploy."}, "what_did_not_work": ["Did not fix: memory is climbing again (193 MB/min), so the restart only treated the symptom"], "escalation": null}

